  "verdict": "Against UniProt ACTIVE SITE features, 17 of 53 annotated positions across 11 comparable entries are confirmed (32%), with 2 UniProt active sites omitted. 1 entries match UniProt's active-site set exactly (O34208) and 0 have none confirmed (none). 5 entries have no UniProt Active site feature at all (P01552, P04419, P0DF97, P13423, P55981), so most of the curation is sourced from structure papers rather than the feature table, which is defensible for toxins and means the omissions are the actionable half, and there are almost none: the only omitted active sites in the whole panel are Q51451's 319 and 343, on the entry already known to be defective. The 32% is also not 68% unsourced. Of the 36 annotated positions that are not Active sites, 17 carry some other UniProt feature, so 34/53 (64%) are grounded in UniProt under some type, which is what a curator reading a structure paper would produce. An earlier version of this audit pooled Binding site and Site with Active site and reported 64 omissions; most of those were carbohydrate, Ca(2+) and cleavage-site features that a catalytic-residue field should not contain, so that number measured the wrong thing. P1 is NOT SUPPORTED (rho -0.221, p 0.514, n 11, underpowered by construction)."
